Subject: [PATCH 93/93] changelog, docs: the PLE_EARLY --tp 2 rank-1 fix is
 confirmed on GPUs (#2)

---
 CHANGELOG.md        | 2 +-
 docs/environment.md | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 058626415..3376ad190 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ Each release's page on GitHub has its notes and measurements. See [the 1.0.0 rel
 
 - Flash Next CUDA: `--pp 2` serves the prompt cache, a state kept at a prompt chunk's mark taking the MTP head's deferred rows first. Each stage keeps its own layers' states (rank 0 also the MTP head's), saved, restored and dropped together over the rank wire as at `--tp 2`, so `--prompt-cache-gib` works as it does on one rank or at `--tp 2` and a returning conversation reuses its prefix. This changes `--pp 2`'s default: its prompt cache was off and a nonzero `--prompt-cache-gib` was refused, and it now takes the same default budget as one rank and `--tp 2` (`--prompt-cache-gib 0` turns it off). Replies are unchanged with or without the cache; `--spill-gib` and `--learn-conversations` are still refused under `--pp` (#2).
 
-- Flash Next CUDA: three default-off switches trim a drafted round's host waits. `TF_FLASHNEXT_PLE_EARLY=1` reads a window's n-gram rows during its draft chain (both ranks at `--tp 2`), `TF_FLASHNEXT_PP_HEAD_SPLIT=1` splits a greedy verify's head between the two `--pp 2` stages, and `TF_FLASHNEXT_ROUND_TURN=1` takes the gather thread's start and the pick's blocking copy off the GPU's path. Known issue: with `TF_FLASHNEXT_PLE_EARLY` at `--tp 2`, a lone stream's greedy replies were not deterministic under agent and mixed traffic; this is traced to rank 1 keeping a served window's rolled history and is fixed in 1645896bb with a host test, but GPU confirmation of the fix is pending (#2).
+- Flash Next CUDA: three default-off switches trim a drafted round's host waits. `TF_FLASHNEXT_PLE_EARLY=1` reads a window's n-gram rows during its draft chain (both ranks at `--tp 2`), `TF_FLASHNEXT_PP_HEAD_SPLIT=1` splits a greedy verify's head between the two `--pp 2` stages, and `TF_FLASHNEXT_ROUND_TURN=1` takes the gather thread's start and the pick's blocking copy off the GPU's path. At `--tp 2`, `TF_FLASHNEXT_PLE_EARLY`'s rank 1 no longer keeps a served window's rolled history, which made a lone stream's greedy replies vary under agent and mixed traffic; the fix (1645896bb, with a host test) is confirmed on 2x RTX PRO 6000, where every lone mixed and agent reply equals the reference with it and the failure reproduces without it (#2).
 
 - Flash Next CUDA: opt-in `TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_OVERLAP` runs a `--tp 2` prompt chunk of at least 2,048 rows as two halves whose expert exchanges run on a side stream and NCCL communicator under the other half's layer, `TF_FLASHNEXT_OWNER_NOCLEAR` skips the owner-slot pass's zero fill of y, and `TF_FLASHNEXT_OVERLAP_OUTPROJ` moves the out projection's gathers to the side stream too; with all three, cold prefill is 42 to 45% faster at 8K, 32K and 128K on 2x RTX PRO 6000 with every token unchanged, at about 2.15 GiB more a rank (`--parallel 14` at a 49152-token window); default serving is unchanged (#2).
 
diff --git a/docs/environment.md b/docs/environment.md
index 36abb080b..77b08c3c6 100644
--- a/docs/environment.md
+++ b/docs/environment.md
@@ -174,7 +174,7 @@ stops the start with the variable, the supplied text and the accepted forms.
 | `TF_FLASHNEXT_PP_WINDOW_GRAPH` | Exactly `0` or `1`; default off. `1`: at `--pp 2` each stage's verify windows run as CUDA graphs with their hop captured, whatever `TF_FLASHNEXT_WINDOW_GRAPH` says; the draft head's graphs still follow `TF_FLASHNEXT_WINDOW_GRAPH`. Same kernels and bits as the eager pass. Give every rank the same value. |
 | `TF_FLASHNEXT_ROLL_BATCH` | Exactly `0` or `1`; default off. `1`: a drafted window's partial keep replays its kept rows over every DeltaNet layer in three launches (all fronts, all chains, all window shifts) instead of about four a layer; the same programs, so replies are unchanged |
 | `TF_FLASHNEXT_SPIN_WAIT` | Exactly `0` or `1`; default off. `1`: at `--tp 2` or `--pp 2`, a host wait for the GPU or NCCL polls without its 50 µs sleeps, which can wake up to about 110 µs after the work is done; each rank keeps one core busy while it waits. Replies are unchanged |
-| `TF_FLASHNEXT_PLE_EARLY` | Exactly `0` or `1`; default off. `1`: a drafted window's n-gram rows are read on the host while its draft chain runs, one token after each pick, so the verify pass copies them and reads only the last token's rows behind layer 0; at `--tp 2` rank 0 sends each token to rank 1, which reads its own copy. The same reads, earlier, so replies are unchanged. Known issue: at `--tp 2` rank 1 read a window after a served one with the same history from stale rows, so replies varied; fixed in 1645896bb, GPU confirmation pending |
+| `TF_FLASHNEXT_PLE_EARLY` | Exactly `0` or `1`; default off. `1`: a drafted window's n-gram rows are read on the host while its draft chain runs, one token after each pick, so the verify pass copies them and reads only the last token's rows behind layer 0; at `--tp 2` rank 0 sends each token to rank 1, which reads its own copy. The same reads, earlier, so replies are unchanged (at `--tp 2` since 1645896bb, confirmed on GPUs under agent and mixed traffic) |
 | `TF_FLASHNEXT_PP_HEAD_SPLIT` | Exactly `0` or `1`; default off. `1`: at `--pp 2` a greedy, unmasked verify scores each half of the vocabulary on one stage from the head both stages hold, and rank 0 merges the two best rows with the same lower-column tie rule as `TF_FLASHNEXT_SHARD_HEAD`. Both ranks must set it alike. Replies are unchanged |
 | `TF_FLASHNEXT_ROUND_TURN` | Exactly `0` or `1`; default off. `1`: a pass's n-gram gather thread starts after its embedding is queued, and a draft pick's best row is copied to pinned memory behind its kernels and polled instead of a stream synchronize and a blocking copy. Replies are unchanged |
 | `TF_FLASHNEXT_PP_SPEC` | Exactly `0` or `1`; default off. `1` on both ranks of `--pp 2` (the ranks refuse to pair otherwise): during rank 1's stage of a lone greedy stream's drafted window, rank 0 runs its layers on a guess at the next window (every draft kept, the draft head's chain on from it) and sends those rows at once when that window is the one verified; a wrong guess is undone on rank 0 alone. The guess runs eagerly whatever the window graph settings say. Replies are unchanged. Inert outside `--pp 2` |
